# Persisting a Multi-Step Form Across Refresh/Crash (Draft Recovery)

## 1. What is it?

This is about **not losing user input** on a long multi-step form (like a job/loan application) when the browser refreshes, crashes, or the tab gets closed accidentally. The fix is **draft persistence**: as the user fills the form, their progress (current step + field values) gets saved to durable client-side storage — typically `localStorage` — on every change. When they come back, the app detects a saved draft and offers to restore it, instead of showing a blank form and forcing them to start over.

## 2. Why was it introduced?

Right now, all form state lives only in memory — in Angular component/service state (or in a `FormGroup`). Memory is wiped the instant the page reloads or the tab dies. For a long form, that's a real cost:

- **Lost work is expensive for the user.** A multi-step application form can take 10-20 minutes to fill. Losing it to an accidental refresh, a crashed tab, or a flaky network reconnect that reloads the page is a genuinely bad experience, and it happens more often than you'd think — trackpad slips, browser extensions triggering a reload, OS updates killing the browser, laptop sleep/wake weirdness.
- **It shows up as support tickets, not just bad UX.** "I filled out the whole form and it disappeared" is a support ticket the team has to handle one by one, and it damages trust in the product — the user has to decide whether to trust the form enough to try again.
- **Long forms already have low completion rates.** Data loss on top of an already-long form makes people abandon entirely rather than redo the work, which is a direct conversion/completion-rate hit for whatever this form gates (signup, application, onboarding).
- **There was no plan for interruption.** The form was built assuming a single, uninterrupted session — but real usage is full of interruptions (refresh, crash, closed tab, switching devices), and none of them were designed for.

## 3. How does it work?

- **Centralize the form's state** in one place — a signal-based service (`providedIn: 'root'`) holding the current step and the field values, rather than scattering state across step components. This makes it possible to save/restore it as a single unit.
- **Auto-save on every change, debounced.** Writing to `localStorage` on every keystroke is wasteful and can visibly stutter typing on slower devices; debounce the writes (e.g., 300-500ms of inactivity) so saves happen in the background without blocking input.
- **Save the *shape* of a draft, not just raw values** — include a schema **version number** alongside the data. If the form's fields change later (a field renamed, removed, or a new required field added), a stale draft that doesn't match the current version can be safely discarded instead of restored into a broken, inconsistent form.
- **Don't silently overwrite on load.** When the app starts and finds a saved draft, don't auto-apply it — ask the user first ("We found a saved draft from 10 minutes ago — Resume or Start Over?"). Silently restoring can be just as jarring as losing data, especially if the user genuinely wanted to start fresh.
- **Clear the draft on successful submission.** Once the form is actually submitted to the backend and accepted, remove the saved draft — otherwise the user gets prompted to "resume" a form they already completed.
- **Persist on every step transition, not just field edits** — moving from step 2 to step 3 should also trigger (or guarantee) a save, in case the user closes the tab right after clicking "Next" before the debounce window fires.
- A **more robust version** of this same idea, for high-value forms, is to also persist the draft to the backend periodically (not just `localStorage`) — this protects against clearing browser data, switching devices, or using a different browser, at the cost of needing a draft-saving API endpoint. `localStorage` alone is the lightweight, no-backend-changes version of the fix.

## 4. Example

**`application-form.service.ts`** — centralized signal-based state, debounced auto-save to `localStorage`, versioned drafts, explicit resume/discard:

```ts
import { Injectable, Injector, signal, runInInjectionContext } from '@angular/core';
import { toObservable } from '@angular/core/rxjs-interop';
import { debounceTime } from 'rxjs/operators';

export interface ApplicationFormData {
  fullName: string;
  email: string;
  employer: string;
  yearsExperience: number | null;
}

interface PersistedDraft {
  version: number;
  step: number;
  data: ApplicationFormData;
  savedAt: string;
}

const DRAFT_KEY = 'application-form-draft';
const SCHEMA_VERSION = 1;

const EMPTY_FORM: ApplicationFormData = {
  fullName: '',
  email: '',
  employer: '',
  yearsExperience: null
};

@Injectable({ providedIn: 'root' })
export class ApplicationFormService {
  step = signal(1);
  data = signal<ApplicationFormData>(EMPTY_FORM);

  draftFound = signal(false);
  lastSavedAt = signal<string | null>(null);

  private pendingDraft: PersistedDraft | null = null;

  constructor(private injector: Injector) {
    this.checkForExistingDraft();
    this.autoSaveOnChange();
  }

  private checkForExistingDraft(): void {
    const raw = localStorage.getItem(DRAFT_KEY);
    if (!raw) return;

    try {
      const parsed: PersistedDraft = JSON.parse(raw);
      if (parsed.version !== SCHEMA_VERSION) {
        // Form shape changed since this draft was saved - don't risk restoring bad data.
        localStorage.removeItem(DRAFT_KEY);
        return;
      }
      this.pendingDraft = parsed;
      this.lastSavedAt.set(parsed.savedAt);
      this.draftFound.set(true); // let the UI ask the user before applying anything
    } catch {
      localStorage.removeItem(DRAFT_KEY); // corrupted JSON - treat as no draft
    }
  }

  private autoSaveOnChange(): void {
    // toObservable + debounceTime needs an injection context, since the service's
    // own constructor context isn't automatically preserved inside the subscribe callback.
    runInInjectionContext(this.injector, () => {
      toObservable(this.data)
        .pipe(debounceTime(400))
        .subscribe(data => this.persist(data));
    });
  }

  private persist(data: ApplicationFormData): void {
    const draft: PersistedDraft = {
      version: SCHEMA_VERSION,
      step: this.step(),
      data,
      savedAt: new Date().toISOString()
    };
    localStorage.setItem(DRAFT_KEY, JSON.stringify(draft));
  }

  updateField<K extends keyof ApplicationFormData>(key: K, value: ApplicationFormData[K]): void {
    this.data.update(current => ({ ...current, [key]: value }));
  }

  goToStep(step: number): void {
    this.step.set(step);
    this.persist(this.data()); // save immediately on navigation too, not just on debounce
  }

  resumeDraft(): void {
    if (!this.pendingDraft) return;
    this.step.set(this.pendingDraft.step);
    this.data.set(this.pendingDraft.data);
    this.draftFound.set(false);
    this.pendingDraft = null;
  }

  discardDraft(): void {
    localStorage.removeItem(DRAFT_KEY);
    this.draftFound.set(false);
    this.pendingDraft = null;
  }

  submit(): void {
    // A real app would POST this.data() to the backend here, and only clear
    // the draft after a successful response.
    localStorage.removeItem(DRAFT_KEY);
    this.step.set(1);
    this.data.set(EMPTY_FORM);
  }
}
```

**`app.component.ts`** — the multi-step UI, with a resume/discard banner:

```ts
import { Component, inject } from '@angular/core';
import { CommonModule } from '@angular/common';
import { ApplicationFormService, ApplicationFormData } from './application-form.service';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-root',
  standalone: true,
  imports: [CommonModule],
  template: `
    <div class="page">
      <h1>Job Application</h1>

      @if (form.draftFound()) {
        <div class="draft-banner">
          <p>We found a saved draft from {{ form.lastSavedAt() }}.</p>
          <button (click)="form.resumeDraft()">Resume</button>
          <button (click)="form.discardDraft()">Start Over</button>
        </div>
      } @else {
        <h2>Step {{ form.step() }} of 3</h2>

        @switch (form.step()) {
          @case (1) {
            <label>Full name
              <input [value]="form.data().fullName"
                     (input)="update('fullName', $any($event.target).value)" />
            </label>
            <label>Email
              <input [value]="form.data().email"
                     (input)="update('email', $any($event.target).value)" />
            </label>
          }
          @case (2) {
            <label>Employer
              <input [value]="form.data().employer"
                     (input)="update('employer', $any($event.target).value)" />
            </label>
            <label>Years of experience
              <input type="number" [value]="form.data().yearsExperience"
                     (input)="update('yearsExperience', +$any($event.target).value)" />
            </label>
          }
          @case (3) {
            <pre>{{ form.data() | json }}</pre>
            <button (click)="form.submit()">Submit application</button>
          }
        }

        <div class="nav">
          @if (form.step() > 1) {
            <button (click)="form.goToStep(form.step() - 1)">Back</button>
          }
          @if (form.step() < 3) {
            <button (click)="form.goToStep(form.step() + 1)">Next</button>
          }
        </div>
      }
    </div>
  `,
  styles: [`
    .page { font-family: sans-serif; padding: 24px; max-width: 420px; }
    label { display: block; margin-bottom: 12px; }
    input { display: block; width: 100%; padding: 6px; margin-top: 4px; }
    .draft-banner { background: #fff3cd; padding: 12px; border-radius: 6px; margin-bottom: 16px; }
    .nav { margin-top: 16px; display: flex; gap: 8px; }
  `]
})
export class AppComponent {
  form = inject(ApplicationFormService);

  update<K extends keyof ApplicationFormData>(key: K, value: ApplicationFormData[K]): void {
    this.form.updateField(key, value);
  }
}
```

